v3.official [51105ccbe]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev3 - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 22 May 2026 19:25:09 +0000 on Wayland - Wayland display driver, Single-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (radeonsi, phoenix, ACO, DRM 3.64, 7.0.9-arch2-1) - AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 28.18 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf I open project A, then open project B in another instance of godot (same godot version), then edit the editor settings in one of them, only the changes done in the editor that closes last will persist.\n\nThis means if I change an editor setting, I have to close all instances (making sure to close the one that I made the change in last), then re-open all the projects\n\nI think this could be fixed by having a \"reload editor settings\" button to read the latest version of the editor settings file, and/or don't write the editor settings to disk if they are unchanged.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a0e4dc5-5094-46b4-986a-f5a3a83f355d\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open a godot project (A)\n- Open another godot project (B)\n- Change an editor setting (like adding a shortcut) in project B\n- Close project B\n- Reload project A\n- The changed setting is lost\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organization